{{Passive skill box|Ghost Dance}}

'''Ghost Dance''' is a keystone on the passive tree. It generates a [[Ghost Shroud]] every two seconds, up to a maximum of three Ghost Shrouds. When [[hit]], a Ghost Shroud is removed and [[recovery|recovers]] energy shield equal to a percentage of your evasion rating.

==Mechanics==
The character must be [[hit]] in order for a Ghost Shroud to recover energy shield. [[receiving damage|Defensive mechanics]] that prevent hits such as [[evasion]] and [[dodge]] will also prevent the loss of Ghost Shrouds. 

[[Hit#Self-damage|Self-hits]] will cause a Ghost Shroud to be lost normally. [[Reflect]]ed hits and [[block]]ed hits will not. Taking damage from blocked hits (e.g. through {{psl|id=glancing_blows_keystone2693}}) does not change this.

While limiting the recovery of energy shield is normally a downside, it could be used to prevent reaching full energy shield, for example to prevent the removal of energy shield [[leech]] instances. 

==Location==
Ghost Dance is located on the top-right side of the tree, on the upper outer parts of the Shadow's starting area.
